## Why TypeScript for credential-channel?

The channel library runs in two places: (1) the browser extension popup and (2) issuer-side web apps. Both are JavaScript environments. Using TypeScript means:
- Single library works everywhere — browser extension, Node.js server, web app
- `tweetnacl` (X25519 + secretbox) is pure JS, no native deps, no WASM needed
- The heavy crypto (Poseidon, BJJ) stays in the protocol's WASM bridge; the channel only does standard ECIES

